#X obj 500 60 switch~;
#X text 300 240 The sound rounded to 6 bits \, 32 steps either side of 0 \, and held at the rate phasor~ runs at \, 22 kHz at drive 0 to 2.8 kHz at 100: [+~ 0.5] \, [wrap~] and [-~] are floor(v + 0.5) \, since vanilla has no round~. Out \, what it changes \, crushed - sound \, which e_drive adds to the sound: so switched off \, as it is for every character but crush \, its output is silence and the sound passes as it is \, and it costs nothing (ref/module/sequencer.md)., f 52;
#X connect 0 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 4 0 6 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 1;
#X connect 6 0 8 0;
#X connect 1 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 1;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 0 0 10 1;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 2 0 12 0;
#X restore 200 620 pd crush;
#X text 20 1040 The curve is one chain for every character: the sound times its gain into [clip~] \, [-~ 0.25] and [cos~] \, a sine of it \, then [*~ k] and a second [clip~]. Soft clips the sine's input at a quarter cycle \, a sine-shaped soft clip. Hard multiplies the sine by 3 and clips it at -0.6 and 1 \, a hard knee \, lopsided. Fold leaves the input unclipped \, so past a quarter cycle the sine folds back. Crush is soft's at 1.5 \, rounded to 6 bits and held at a lower rate in pd crush. So a character is five numbers \, a trim and whether it crushes \, and choosing one costs nothing. hip~ 15 takes out the DC a lopsided clip leaves. No oversampling: a clipped drum's aliasing is part of its edge (Reference \, pure-data \, Distortion)., f 60;
#X text 600 1040 The gain scales the sound to its sample's peak \, so a drive means the same on every pad: the peak goes in at an eighth of a cycle at drive 0 \, ten times that at 50 and a hundred at 100 (crush: a range of ten). The makeup falls with the drive as 1 over the root of that gain \, but only to -8 dB \, then holds (crush: -6 dB) \, times the peak again and the character's trim: so more drive is louder and dirtier \, never quieter. tone is the low-pass's cutoff \, 300 Hz at 0 to 18 kHz at 100 \, even in octaves. Every value has its starting point in its box: soft \, drive 50 \, tone 100 \, a peak of 1. None is set at load: c_steps tells c_kit every effect's value at load \, and c_voice the peak once its sample is read (ref/module/sequencer.md)., f 50;
#X text 1000 1300 switch~ keeps it off while the mix is 0 \, so a track with no distortion costs nothing \, and in c_voice \, which is itself off while its voice is silent \, one with it costs only while its voice sounds. A switch~ starts off \, and so does pd crush's own \, on only while the character is crush., f 40;
